<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dmitrov</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dmitrov is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> Oblast, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, about 65 kilometres north of Moscow. It was founded in 1154 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-dolgoruky">Yuri Dolgoruky</a>, who named it after the patron saint of his newborn son Vsevolod, baptised Dmitry. Its earthen ramparts and 16th-century Cathedral of the Dormition survive, and it later served as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of Moscow princes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dmitrov.jpg" alt="Dmitrov" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mike1979 Russia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dmitrov_Church_of_the_Dormition_2023-09-23_8718.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
